## 0. Big picture in plain English

We’re doing this only for **one product: VNP** (Vision+ cards).

### Tables you will have (5)

All will be in BigQuery, in one dataset, e.g. `merge_match_dev`.

1. **`vnp_accounts_mock`** – COG account table (one row per account)
2. **`credit_facility_mock`** – main BOLT facility info (one row per facility instance)
3. **`mapped_facility_mock`** – tells which source system a facility came from
4. **`fulfilled_account_mock`** – links a facility instance to an account id
5. **`facility_purpose_mock`** – describes why the facility exists (purpose text)

### Core keys

* `ACCOUNT_NUMBER` – account identifier in COG
* `fulfilledAccountId` – account identifier in FulfilledAccount
* `facilityInstanceId` – main facility key across facility tables

**Join chain:**

```text
COG VNP account (ACCOUNT_NUMBER)
   ↕ (matches)
FulfilledAccount.fulfilledAccountId
   ↕ facilityInstanceId
CreditFacility.facilityInstanceId
   ↕ facilityInstanceId
MappedFacility + FacilityPurpose
```

Dataflow job will:

1. Read all 5 tables
2. Join them using these keys
3. Produce a new table: **`vnp_account_facility_single_view`**

